From 2023c41e67066cebcfd5b3720790b5105171a827 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: praveen <praveenkumar.shanmugam@amd.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:54:47 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] GPUOP-1130: Implement per-attribute cadence tiers in
 smi-watcher

Per-attribute cadence on the existing 1 s smi-watcher timer (GPUOP-1122
rev 3, code paths power-thread-and-tiers: tiers + tick plan, and
amdsmi-watcher: sweep). The POWER tier stays watcher-owned
(power_by_watcher always true) until the smi-power thread lands in
GPUOP-1131; sub-second periods stay OP_NOT_SUPPORTED.

- smi_watch: GPU_WATCH_TIER_POWER; k_power_attrs holds the 13 POWER ids
  (68/69/70, 126, 139 and 141/142 from k_fast_attrs; 90-95 from
  k_slow_attrs). FAST keeps every other fast attr plus 140 UBB_POWER;
  SLOW keeps every other slow attr. smi_watch_attr_tier() (for the power
  thread / frame code in GPUOP-1131/1132)
- periods are std::atomic<uint32_t>; smi_watch_fast_period() (seconds)
  is replaced by gpu_watch_tick_plan_t {fast_due, slow_due,
  power_by_watcher} and smi_watch_tick_plan(): uint32 ms accumulators,
  fast due at max(fast_ms, 1000), slow due on fast-due ticks at
  slow_secs * 1000 or on the first published sample. Identical to the
  old uint16 tick counters at whole-second periods
- shared smi_watch_fill_power_fields(const amdsmi_gpu_metrics_t *,
  fields *) (AMD_SMI): 126 widen-NA, 139 x energy resolution (15.3
  fallback), 68-70 widen-NA, 90-95 and 141/142 as is
- aga_gpu_watch_reset_power_fields() resets the 13 POWER fields to
  UINT64_MAX; aga_gpu_watch_reset_fast_fields() no longer resets them
  or UBB 140
- smi_state: slow_cache_ -> watch_rec_; watcher_update_watch_db and the
  per-GPU sweep take the tick plan
- amdsmi sweep: seeds from watch_rec_, resets FAST (+POWER when
  watcher-owned), fills POWER from the bulk gpu_metrics read through the
  helper (90-95 now from that read and refreshed every fast tick;
  amdsmi_get_violation_status is still read on slow ticks for the PCT
  and GFX-clock violation attrs), skips POWER cases in the attr loop and
  writes watch_rec_ back every fast tick. The DB-update task is posted
  from a preallocated static task spec
- UBB 140 (GPUOP-1124 hook): 1 s floor, FAST tier, so
  amdsmi_get_power_info runs at most once per FAST tick for probed
  partition-0 handles; the value is no longer reset every tick, it is
  carried in watch_rec_ and set to NA only when the read fails or
  returns 0; non-probed handles are NA (never 0)
- GIM / WSL: tick plan; reset POWER fields every fast tick (watcher
  always owns them). WSL keeps its own fills and keeps 90-95 from the
  slow-tick violation read, carried from the last slow snapshot. GIM
  90-95 were never filled and are now NA instead of 0

Build and mock verification run in the exporter CI.

